# JuliaXSPEC: XSPEC local models written in Julia

References:
- [XSPEC Appendix C: Adding Models to XSPEC](https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/docs/software/xspec/manual/XSappendixLocal.html) (`model.dat`, `initpackage`, `hmake`, `lmod`)
- [OGIP 92-009 table model format](https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/FTP/caldb/docs/memos/ogip_92_009/ogip_92_009.pdf)
- [PackageCompiler.jl `create_library`](https://julialang.github.io/PackageCompiler.jl/stable/libs.html)

## Conventions that must not drift

- A model returns **photons cm⁻² s⁻¹ per bin** (`BinnedSpectrum.per_bin`), never a density. `density`/`from_density` convert explicitly. See `docs/src/units.md`.
- Convolution kernels `L(g)` have **unit area in g** (photon conservation). See `docs/src/convolution.md` for the derivation that the code follows.
- XSPEC reads the `model.dat` init string as a **single token**; configuration goes through `JULIAXSPEC_*` environment variables (`src/options.jl`).
- C wrapper names are the model name with underscores removed; `model.dat` refers to them as `c_<name>`.
- `register!` must be called from a module's `__init__`, not at top level (precompilation).

## Architecture

- `src/entry.jl`: the single `@ccallable juliaxspec_evaluate`; never lets an exception reach C.
- `src/registry.jl`: registry plus generation of `xspec/model.dat` and `xspec/juliaxspec_wrappers.c`. Both generated files are tracked; CI checks they match the models.
- `models/`: the model set compiled into `build/lib/libjuliaxspec_models`. Add models there (or in a dependent package) and rebuild.
- `scripts/compile.jl`: PackageCompiler build; `scripts/patch_xspec_makefile.jl`: adds our link flags to the Makefile `initpackage` writes.

## Build and verify

```sh
./build-julia.sh      # Julia only: compile models, write xspec/model.dat and wrappers
./build-xspec.sh      # HEADAS required: initpackage + patch + hmake in xspec/
xspec                 # lmod juliaxspec xspec
cd verification && xspec - phase1.xcm && julia --project=. compare.jl
```

Rebuild the Julia library after any change in `src/` or `models/`; rebuild the XSPEC package only when `model.dat` changes. Keep platform-specific workarounds out of the build scripts unless a reproducible failure requires one.
